From d4cd19847bc4e7340c9b7b870cf8f8bd777f2a09 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: well0nez <8986239+well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 02:06:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 09/87] h713: dram: self-refresh, ported from the vendor's DRAM
 standby driver V1.15

The vendor ARISC firmware's enter side (blob 0x142dc) and exit side
(0x145b0 -> 0x14004 -> 0x13884 and its helpers), register by register:
the save area 0x16d9c field by field, PWRCTL 0x101 and STATR == 3, CKEN
off, DX/AC pads to CMOS and off, pad hold (R_PRCM 0x250), DRAM clocks and
PLL_DDR0 off; on the way back the ZQ path by tpr13/tpr9, PLL_DDR0 and the
DRAM clock rebuilt, IOVCR from tpr5/tpr6, the COM +0x500 group by type and
SID chip id, MR0..3, the saved timing and PHY delay registers, refresh
timing from 7800/350 ns, PIR 0x62 (no DRAM init, no training), the
PWRCTL toggle out of self-refresh, PGSR0's error bits, then the tail
(auto self-refresh by tpr13 bit 30, PGCR0, ZQCR, 0xb8, 0x108, 0x7c).

The DRAM parameters are Kconfig (HY310 defaults from U-Boot's
hy310_defconfig: DDR3, 792 MHz, tpr13 0xb4016103) and the whole port sits
behind H713_DRAM_SELF_REFRESH (default n): h713_hy310_sr_defconfig is the
image that uses it. Checked offline only: skripte/dram_trace.py
(crust-20261007) runs the blob's routines and these in one register model
- identical access lists (address, value, order) for the HY310 parameters
with five SID chip ids and for two parameter sets that take the LPDDR3,
gate mode 1/2, ZQ calibration and half-width branches; the only difference
is the blob's read of 0x0300016c for a log line. Not run on a device.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 configs/h713_hy310_sr_defconfig |   9 +
 drivers/dram/sun50i-h713-dram.c | 441 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
